  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Creating an enabling environment for the establishment and enhancement of regular labour pathways from Kyrgyzstan to the European Union</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Recent geopolitical developments have led to an increase in return migration to Kyrgyzstan, mainly from the Russian Federation. In parallel, there is increased evidence of a diversification of destination countries for Kyrgyz labour migrants, particularly in the European Union (EU), such as Bulgaria, Hungary, Lithuania or Slovakia. However, existing regular labour pathways are not sufficiently people-centred, rights-based, safe and accessible, and there is a lack of coordination among national and cross-national entities relevant for the establishment, operationalization and enhancement of regular labour pathways. The objective of the project is to contribute to the establishment and enhancement of regular labour mobility pathways for a safe, orderly and regular migration from Kyrgyzstan to countries in the EU. The Government of Kyrgyzstan and relevant stakeholders will take measures to adopt a whole-of-government and whole-of-society coordination mechanism and a gender-sensitive Labour Mobility Roadmap that enable a facilitating environment for safe and orderly regular labour mobility pathways to the EU.</narrative>
  </description>
